  "history_of_present_illness": "The patient is a 69\u2011year\u2011old woman with a long\u2011standing history of essential hypertension, obesity, and progressive glucose dysregulation that began as pre\u2011diabetes in the early 1970s and has since evolved to type 2 diabetes mellitus treated with insulin. Diabetic kidney disease manifested as micro\u2011albuminuria in the 1970s, progressed to proteinuria in the 1980s and is now classified as chronic kidney disease stage 4. She is listed for kidney transplantation. Blood pressure is low (97/56\u202fmmHg) likely secondary to a three\u2011drug antihypertensive regimen (lisinopril, hydrochlorothiazide, amlodipine). The most recent A1c of 3.2\u202f% is unusually low and may reflect overtreatment or a laboratory error. Additional chronic issues include intractable migraine, chronic sinusitis, chronic stress, and a history of miscarriage. Socially she works part\u2011time, has a criminal record, and a resolved history of intimate partner abuse.",
